# polkit < 0.106 (e.g. Ubuntu 22.04, which ships polkit 0.105) reads .pkla
# files, NOT the JavaScript .rules twin in
# ../../rules.d/50-polaris-update.rules. Without this the one-click
# self-update fails with an authorization ("policy rules") error on those
# systems. Newer polkit ignores this file and honours the .rules instead,
# so shipping both is safe: each system uses the format it understands.
#
# Unlike the JS rule, a .pkla cannot scope to a single unit (it matches by
# action id, not by the unit name), so here the polaris user gets
# manage-units for any unit. Acceptable: the appliance's polaris user is
# already in the sudo group.
[Polaris passwordless self-update (polkit < 0.106)]
Identity=unix-user:polaris
Action=org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage-units;org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage-unit-files
ResultAny=yes
ResultInactive=yes
ResultActive=yes
